# InsolventEstateAbatement — pari passu abatement of an insolvent estate's debts

Where a deceased person's estate is insolvent (the debts exceed the assets available
to pay them), the estate is administered under the insolvency regime: the Administration
of Insolvent Estates of Deceased Persons Order 1986 (SI 1986/1999) applies the Insolvency
Act 1986 to the administration of a deceased insolvent estate. Insolvency Act 1986 s.328(3)
states that debts of the same rank "rank equally between themselves, and shall be paid in
full unless the assets are insufficient for meeting them, in which case they abate in equal
proportions between themselves" — the pari passu principle. This scope computes that equal-
proportion abatement across a single rank of unsecured creditors: each creditor receives its
claim multiplied by the ratio of available assets to total claims (capped at payment in full
when the estate is solvent).

Legal correctness is asserted outside this file by the T032 per-heir gov-oracle harness
(TT-478 pattern): code-inherit-test-suite/scripts/oracle_verify.py runs the Abate scope, reads
the per-creditor list per_member field abated_payments, and compares it against
tests/oracles/insolvent-estate-abatement.oracle.json — including a wrong_split negative case
that must turn the harness RED if a right-total/wrong-split answer ever matched. This file
therefore carries the abatement law, not its own per-creditor assertions; the NeedsHuman branch
(which the per-heir harness cannot assert) is proven by the in-file test scope below.

(Prose note: a line must not begin with the reserved directive prefix, so any statutory
quotation is kept inline.)

MVP scope boundary — single unsecured rank only. creditor_claims is the list of same-rank
unsecured claims, each a whole-GBP integer (lifted to money in-rule so the per-heir harness,
which renders a list only as bare integers, can supply it). available_assets is the fund
available to that rank after any higher-ranking claims. Secured and preferential creditors
(Insolvency Act 1986 s.328(1) + Schedule 6) rank AHEAD of the pari passu rank and are out of
MVP scope: where has_preferential_or_secured is set, the split is not computable from these
inputs alone and the scope returns NeedsHuman. Interest on the debts (s.328(4)-(5)) and the
statutory order of application of assets for a SOLVENT estate (AEA 1925 s.34(3), Part II
Schedule 1) are out of MVP scope.

G6 certification floor (TT-427/TT-1079): every input is a characterisation judgement
(`registry/governance-layers.yaml`, all L3 — claim validity, asset valuation, debt-rank
classification), so each arrives as a `ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Certified<Type>` enum; any
uncertified input routes `NeedsHuman` via the `uncertified_inputs` gate before a split is
reachable, and the `_v` extraction fallbacks are dead code guarded by that gate.

```catala
declaration scope Abate:
  input available_assets content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney
  input creditor_claims content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList
  input has_preferential_or_secured content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool
  internal uncertified_inputs content boolean
  internal available_assets_v content money
  internal creditor_claims_v content list of integer
  internal has_preferential_or_secured_v content boolean
  internal claim_amounts content list of money
  internal total_claims content money
  internal is_insolvent content boolean
  internal abatement_ratio content decimal
  output abated_payments content list of money
  output verdict content ComputedOrNeedsHuman.Verdict

scope Abate:
  definition uncertified_inputs equals
    (match available_assets with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match creditor_claims with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: true)
    or (match has_preferential_or_secured with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: false -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: true)
  definition available_assets_v equals
    match available_assets with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.NotCharacterised: $0
  definition creditor_claims_v equals
    match creditor_claims with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.NotCharacterised: []
  definition has_preferential_or_secured_v equals
    match has_preferential_or_secured with pattern -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content v: v -- ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.NotCharacterised: false
  # lift each whole-GBP integer claim to money
  definition claim_amounts equals
    map each c among creditor_claims_v to ($1 * (decimal of c))
  definition total_claims equals sum money of claim_amounts
  definition is_insolvent equals total_claims > available_assets_v
  # pari passu ratio: assets/total when insolvent, else full payment (1.0)
  definition abatement_ratio equals
    if is_insolvent then available_assets_v / total_claims else 1.0
  definition abated_payments equals
    if uncertified_inputs then []
    else map each m among claim_amounts to (m * abatement_ratio)
  definition verdict equals
    if uncertified_inputs then NeedsHuman
    else if has_preferential_or_secured_v then NeedsHuman
    else Computed content (sum money of abated_payments)
```

## In-file tests — the Computed pari-passu split and the NeedsHuman branch

The per-heir harness asserts the Computed split externally but cannot render the NeedsHuman
branch (it carries no per-creditor list); both arms are proven here.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPariPassuComputed:
  output payments content list of money
  output is_computed content boolean

scope TestPariPassuComputed:
  definition payments equals
    (output of Abate with {
      -- available_assets: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $60,000
      -- creditor_claims: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content [30000; 30000; 40000]
      -- has_preferential_or_secured: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
    }).abated_payments
  definition is_computed equals
    match (output of Abate with {
      -- available_assets: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $60,000
      -- creditor_claims: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content [30000; 30000; 40000]
      -- has_preferential_or_secured: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content false
    }).verdict with pattern
    -- Computed content m: true
    -- NeedsHuman: false
  assertion is_computed = true
  assertion payments = [$18,000; $18,000; $24,000]

#[test]
declaration scope TestPreferentialNeedsHuman:
  output is_needs_human content boolean

scope TestPreferentialNeedsHuman:
  definition is_needs_human equals
    match (output of Abate with {
      -- available_assets: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedMoney.Certified content $60,000
      -- creditor_claims: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedIntegerList.Certified content [30000; 30000; 40000]
      -- has_preferential_or_secured: ComputedOrNeedsHuman.CertifiedBool.Certified content true
    }).verdict with pattern
    -- Computed content m: false
    -- NeedsHuman: true
  assertion is_needs_human = true
```
